@startuml
title ActiveHub implemented booking, compensation and delivery collaboration
actor User
participant "Next route + handler" as Route
participant "bookings.createBooking" as Booking
participant "seatPolicy / SeatPolicy\nStrategy" as Policy
participant "loyalty.quoteBooking\nPriceStep chain" as Price
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "payments.payBooking\nSimulatedCardGateway Adapter" as Pay
participant "bookings.transition" as Transition
participant "worker / email-outbox" as Worker
participant "SmtpMailTransport\nAdapter" as Mail
User -> Route : DTO + cookies + CSRF + idempotency key
Route -> Booking
Booking -> DB : transaction, role/owner checks, event/session locks
Booking -> Policy : ordinary / single participant / exclusive hall
Booking -> Price : promotion -> free quota -> card discount
Price -> DB : card lock, session-month quota usage
Booking -> DB : reserve seats/visits/quota, snapshot price, history
Booking -> DB : in-app notice, outbox, idempotency response; commit
opt Positive card payment
 User -> Pay : card credentials in memory only
 Pay -> DB : same lock order, one payment, last4 only
 Pay -> Transition : CONFIRMED
 Transition -> DB : award points once, notifications; commit
end
opt Allowed cancellation / rejection / expiry
 User -> Transition
 Transition -> DB : release quota, return visits, reverse original points
 Transition -> DB : full payment refund once, terminal status/history, notices
end
Worker -> DB : claim committed outbox row, persistent retry state
Worker -> Mail : rendered text/HTML, stable Message-ID
Mail -> DB : record delivery / retry / permanent failure
note over DB,Mail
Q-01 reversal clamps at zero; Q-02 uses the session month in Europe/Kyiv.
Q-03 cutoff is inclusive; Q-04 corporate eligibility lasts until calendar expiry.
External SMTP exactly-once delivery is not claimed.
end note
@enduml
